Terminal 1 — CAN bus (one time)


sudo ip link set can0 up type can bitrate 250000
ip link show can0
Terminal 2 — full stack (MoveIt + ros2_control + hardware)


source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash
source /home/smallpapaya/SKAI_ws/install/setup.bash
ros2 launch skai_control moveit_controller.launch.py
Wait until you see:


[moveit_controller_node]: MoveIt controller ready
[skai_hardware]: ODrive CLOSED_LOOP sent
Terminal 3 — dashboard GUI


source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash
source /home/smallpapaya/SKAI_ws/install/setup.bash
ros2 run skai_dashboard dashboard
Verify in the GUI

What to check Expected
Left panel LEDs Turn green (closed loop, data flowing)
Right panel joint cards Show live rad and turns values from encoder
Controller status arm_controller ACTIVE in green
3D visualizer Arm drawn at current joint positions
Test IK — in the center panel, enter X=0.30  Y=0.00  Z=0.40 and click SEND IK GOAL. Watch the 3D arm move to the planned pose.

Test E-STOP — click the red button. LEDs turn yellow (online but inactive). Click RESUME to re-arm.